// Veridian/C-like code snippet from the Aethelgard Archive's TerraOS
int SensorSync(int sensor_id, unsigned long pressure_reading) {
    unsigned long adjusted_pressure;

    if (sensor_id == 7) { // APR-7 Sensor
        adjusted_pressure = pressure_reading * calibration_factor; // calibration_factor is a constant, e.g., 2
        if (adjusted_pressure > MAX_PRESSURE) {
            // Safety check - Should prevent the lock from disengaging
            return -1; // Error code
        }
        vault_pressure = adjusted_pressure; // Assign to the global variable
    } else {
        return -2; // Invalid sensor ID
    }

    if (vault_pressure > CRITICAL_THRESHOLD) {
        bypass_lock(); // Trigger the bypass if pressure is too high
    }

    return 0; // Success
}
```

Elara, having access to the source code (or a disassembled version) would see this. Her exploit isn't writing new code, but crafting a `pressure_reading` value that circumvents the `MAX_PRESSURE` check.  She’s using a tool to inject this crafted value.  On her terminal:

